  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bakelite is a thermosetting plastic which is formed by the reaction of phenol with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>CHO</mi></math> in the presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> (conc).</p><p>The reaction occurs as follows:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/2c748085-481d-4449-8dd7-151e7fcde4bf-image.png\" style=\"width: 823px; height: 242px;\" /></p><p>A cross-linked condensation polymer (at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></math>-and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>-position) bakelite is thus produced.</p>",
